WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.668
[car horns blaring]

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:04.304
[phone ringing]

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:11.511
[jungle wildlife calls]

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.078
OPERATOR (THROUGH PHONE):
Prepaid call from.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.481
JOE EXOTIC (THROUGH
PHONE): Joe Exotic.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.815
OPERATOR (THROUGH
PHONE): An inmate

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.350
at the Grady County Jail.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:20.553
This call is also subject to
being recorded or monitored.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.888
JOE EXOTIC (THROUGH
PHONE): Hello?

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:22.921
Hi, how are you doing?

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.057
Mariana here.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.191
JOE EXOTIC (THROUGH PHONE): Hi.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.026
Thank you so much
for calling me.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.161
MARIANA (VOICEOVER):
It all started

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.696
with an online reality show.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:32.932
Hey, I'm Joe Exotic,
The gay, gun-carrying

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.501
redneck with a mullet.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.369
MARIANA (VOICEOVER): Before
Netflix's hit series,

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:40.373
"Tiger King" made Joe
Exotic famous worldwide.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.474
FILMMAKER: He was like a
mythical character living out

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.444
in the middle of
[beep] Oklahoma.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.945
MARIANA (VOICEOVER):
But lost in the hype

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.714
surrounding the series--

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.550
MAN: So Joe said, will you
go to Florida and what?

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.218
HIT-MAN: Kill that [beep] lady.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.686
MARIANA (VOICEOVER):
--was a serious discussion

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:57.056
about private tiger
ownership in America.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.291
JOE EXOTIC (THROUGH PHONE):
I've been in the tiger industry

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.561
for a little over 20 years now.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.831
Probably the largest
breeder and handler

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.666
of tigers in the United States.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:11.905
MARIANA: So give me just a
sense of the tiger community,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.473
cow petting zoos, and all that.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.074
JOE EXOTIC (THROUGH PHONE):
Well, you're getting the world

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.042
to pay for your hobby.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.210
Yeah.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.745
JOE EXOTIC (THROUGH
PHONE): At least

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.713
that we have man enough to
say, look, I own a roadside zoo

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.682
and I breed tigers.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.752
I'm stuck trying to
figure out why the hell

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.887
I'm in jail, for first of all.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.288
MARIANA (VOICEOVER):
To be clear,

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.691
Joey Exotic is behind bars
because he was convicted

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:35.994
of the attempted murder
for hire of Carole Baskin

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:38.832
as well as 17 wildlife crimes.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.701
CARNEY ANNE NASSER: In the words
of the judge at Joe Exotic's

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:46.573
sentencing, Joe is a master
manipulator who is engaged in,

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:51.344
quote, "systematic trafficking"
of tigers and other big cats.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.012
MARIANA (VOICEOVER): Yet,
critics of "Tiger King"

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:57.015
say the series celebrated
Joe, while largely overlooking

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.618
his treatment of animals.

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:01.688
CARNEY ANNE NASSER:
Joe is not a folk hero.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:05.358
He is somebody who, for
decades, profited off

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:08.127
of the exploitation
and abuse of animals.

00:02:08.193 --> 00:02:11.331
And Joe is finally
where he belongs.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.432
MARIANA (VOICEOVER):
So why would

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:14.400
you want to breed a tiger?

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:18.404
Well, in the US roadside
zoos can bring in big money

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:22.008
by offering cow petting
experiences to tourists.

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.209
JOHN GOODRICH: They raise
tiger cubs, so that people can

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.012
pay money and take
selfies, so they

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.580
have to have this
constant supply

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:32.584
of these little tiny tiger cubs
between one and four months.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.421
So there's just this
huge breeding operation,

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.658
but the key thing here is
that after the cubs are about

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:41.661
four-months-old, they're
too dangerous for the public

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:42.662
to handle.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.864
They need to be
handed off somewhere.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.132
And often, I don't
think we really

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.433
know what happens to them.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.902
MARIANA (VOICEOVER):
To understand the scope

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:52.105
of the issue, "National
Geographic" magazine reviewed

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:56.309
Joe Exotic's records
from 2010 to 2018,

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.044
and learned that his
zoo traded nearly

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:03.516
200 tigers with dozens of other
private owners across America.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.752
Breeders, like Joe,
are one of the reasons

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:09.355
that they are now an
estimated 5 to 10,000

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.425
tigers in the United States.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:15.495
With less than 4,000
tigers left in the wild,

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:19.399
there are now more tigers
living in captivity in the US

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.401
than there are
wild tigers living

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.002
in the rest of the world.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.004
JOE EXOTIC (THROUGH PHONE): If
something's endangered, hell,

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.806
we need to start
breeding it, do we not?

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:30.176
Is that not what the purpose
of it being endangered is?

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.846
We need more of.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:37.283
[ominous music playing]

